1
00:00:02,360 --> 00:00:09,580
Chapter 35 He did not leave for Cambridge the next day, as he had said he would.

2
00:00:10,399 --> 00:00:15,580
He deferred his departure a whole week, and during that time he made me feel what

3
00:00:15,581 --> 00:00:19,876
severe punishment a good yet stern, a conscientious yet

4
00:00:19,877 --> 00:00:23,500
implacable man can inflict on one who has offended him.

5
00:00:24,460 --> 00:00:31,000
Without one overt act of hostility, one upgrading word, he contrived to

6
00:00:31,001 --> 00:00:36,399
impress me momently, with the conviction that I was put beyond the pale of his

7
00:00:36,400 --> 00:00:42,380
favour, not that Sinjin harbored a spirit of un-Christian vindictiveness,

8
00:00:43,399 --> 00:00:45,836
not that he would have injured a hair of my

9
00:00:45,838 --> 00:00:49,320
head if it had been fully in his power to do so.

10
00:00:50,380 --> 00:00:53,941
Chapter 3 Both by nature and principle, he was

11
00:00:53,942 --> 00:00:57,561
superior to the mean gratification of vengeance.

12
00:00:58,479 --> 00:01:04,059
He had forgiven me for saying I scorned him and his love, but he had not forgotten

13
00:01:04,061 --> 00:01:09,080
the words, and as long as he and I lived, he never would forget them.

14
00:01:09,740 --> 00:01:13,459
I saw by his look, when he turned to me, that they

15
00:01:13,460 --> 00:01:16,720
were always written on the air between me and him.

16
00:01:17,919 --> 00:01:22,312
When ever I spoke, they sounded in my voice to his

17
00:01:22,312 --> 00:01:25,800
ear, and their echo toned every answer he gave me.

18
00:01:26,759 --> 00:01:29,619
He did not abstain from conversing with me.

19
00:01:30,460 --> 00:01:36,339
He even called me as usual each morning to join him at his desk, and I fear the

20
00:01:36,341 --> 00:01:39,646
corrupt man within him had a pleasure un

21
00:01:39,648 --> 00:01:43,960
-imparted too, and unshared by the pure Christian.

22
00:01:44,179 --> 00:01:49,360
In a vinceing with what skill he could, while acting and speaking, apparently just

23
00:01:49,361 --> 00:01:55,479
as usual, extract from every deed and every phrase, the spirit of interest and

24
00:01:55,480 --> 00:01:58,328
approval, which had formerly communicated a

25
00:01:58,330 --> 00:02:01,941
certain austere charm to his language and manner.

26
00:02:02,300 --> 00:02:06,940
To me, he was in reality become no longer flesh, but marble.

27
00:02:07,559 --> 00:02:09,699
His eye was a cold, bright.

28
00:02:10,179 --> 00:02:11,179
Blue gem.

29
00:02:11,460 --> 00:02:13,179
His tongue a speaking instrument.

30
00:02:14,039 --> 00:02:15,039
Nothing more.

31
00:02:15,500 --> 00:02:19,259
All this was torture to me, refined lingering torture.

32
00:02:20,199 --> 00:02:24,024
It kept up a slow fire of indignation and a trembling

33
00:02:24,025 --> 00:02:27,300
trouble of grief, which harassed and crushed me altogether.

34
00:02:28,100 --> 00:02:33,539
I felt how, if I were his wife, this good man, pure as the deep,

35
00:02:33,820 --> 00:02:38,580
sunless source could soon kill me, without drawing from my veins a single

36
00:02:38,581 --> 00:02:41,726
drop of blood, or receiving on his own crystal

37
00:02:41,728 --> 00:02:45,260
conscience the faintest stain of crime.

38
00:02:45,539 --> 00:02:50,380
Especially I felt this when I made any attempt to propitiate him.

39
00:02:51,380 --> 00:02:52,779
No Ruth met my Ruth.

40
00:02:53,259 --> 00:02:57,740
He experienced no suffering from a strangement, no yearning after

41
00:02:57,740 --> 00:03:03,979
reconciliation, and though, more than once, my fast-falling tears blistered the

42
00:03:03,980 --> 00:03:10,139
page over which we both bent, they produced no more effect on him than if his

43
00:03:10,141 --> 00:03:13,500
heart had been really a matter of stone or metal.

44
00:03:14,580 --> 00:03:16,899
To his sisters mean time.

45
00:03:17,860 --> 00:03:23,419
He was somewhat kinder than usual, as if afraid that mere coldness would not

46
00:03:23,421 --> 00:03:28,539
sufficiently convince me how completely I was banished and banned.

47
00:03:29,300 --> 00:03:34,880
He added the force of contrast, and this I am sure he did not by malice,

48
00:03:35,479 --> 00:03:36,479
but on principle.

49
00:03:37,639 --> 00:03:42,039
The night before he left home, happening to see him walking in the garden

50
00:03:42,040 --> 00:03:47,759
about sunset, and remembering, as I looked at him, that this man,

51
00:03:48,520 --> 00:03:54,860
alienated as he now was, had once saved my life and that we were near relations,

52
00:03:55,699 --> 00:03:59,639
I was moved to make a last attempt to regain his friendship.

53
00:04:00,699 --> 00:04:03,941
I went out, and approached him as he stood leaning

54
00:04:03,941 --> 00:04:06,941
over the little gate, I spoke to the point at once.

55
00:04:07,500 --> 00:04:12,360
Sinjin, I am unhappy because you are still angry with me, let us be friends.

56
00:04:14,119 --> 00:04:20,759
I hope we are friends, was the unmoved reply, while he still watched the rising

57
00:04:20,760 --> 00:04:24,380
of the moon, which he had been contemplating as I approached.

58
00:04:25,660 --> 00:04:29,619
No, Sinjin, we are not friends as we were, you know that.

59
00:04:30,399 --> 00:04:31,399
Are we not?

60
00:04:32,020 --> 00:04:33,020
That is wrong.

61
00:04:33,779 --> 00:04:36,940
For my part, I wish you no ill and all good.

62
00:04:37,860 --> 00:04:42,919
I believe you, Sinjin, for I am sure you are incapable of wishing anyone ill,

63
00:04:43,479 --> 00:04:48,660
but as I am your kin's woman, I should desire somewhat more of affection than

64
00:04:48,660 --> 00:04:52,399
that sort of general philanthropy you extend to mere strangers.

65
00:04:53,679 --> 00:04:57,508
Of course, he said, your wish is reasonable,

66
00:04:57,509 --> 00:05:00,620
and I am far from regarding you as a stranger.

67
00:05:02,179 --> 00:05:07,800
This, spoken in a cool tranquil tone, was mortifying and baffling enough,

68
00:05:08,720 --> 00:05:13,220
had I attended to the suggestions of pride and anger, I should immediately have left

69
00:05:13,221 --> 00:05:17,380
him, but something worked within me more strongly than those feelings could.

70
00:05:18,339 --> 00:05:21,639
I deeply venerated my cousin's talent and principle.

71
00:05:22,720 --> 00:05:27,720
His friendship was a value to me, to lose it, tried me severely.

72
00:05:28,279 --> 00:05:31,639
I would not so soon relinquish the attempt to reconquer it.

73
00:05:32,600 --> 00:05:34,740
Must we part in this way, Sinjin?

74
00:05:35,639 --> 00:05:38,603
And when you go to India, will you leave me so,

75
00:05:38,604 --> 00:05:41,980
without a kinder word than you have yet spoken?

76
00:05:43,020 --> 00:05:46,039
He now turned quite from the moon and faced me.

77
00:05:47,199 --> 00:05:49,380
When I go to India, Jane, will I leave you?

78
00:05:49,979 --> 00:05:50,979
What?

79
00:05:51,039 --> 00:05:52,320
Do you not go to India?

80
00:05:53,259 --> 00:05:58,160
You said I could not, unless I married you, and you will not marry me?

81
00:05:58,899 --> 00:06:00,479
You adhere to that resolution?

82
00:06:01,479 --> 00:06:05,101
Rita, do you know as I do, what terror those cold

83
00:06:05,103 --> 00:06:08,240
people can put into the ice of their questions?

84
00:06:09,100 --> 00:06:12,657
How much of the fall of the avalanches in their anger, of

85
00:06:12,657 --> 00:06:15,759
the breaking up of the frozen sea in their displeasure?

86
00:06:16,899 --> 00:06:20,360
No, Sinjin, I will not marry you.

87
00:06:20,820 --> 00:06:22,240
I adhere to my resolution.

88
00:06:23,440 --> 00:06:29,740
The avalanche had shaken and slurred a little forward, but it did not yet crash down.

89
00:06:30,080 --> 00:06:33,460
Once more, why this refusal, he asked?

90
00:06:35,500 --> 00:06:39,339
Formerly, I answered, because you did not love me.

91
00:06:40,160 --> 00:06:43,419
Now I reply, because you almost hate me.

92
00:06:44,320 --> 00:06:46,660
If I were to marry you, you would kill me.

93
00:06:47,500 --> 00:06:48,600
You are killing me now.

94
00:06:49,059 --> 00:06:50,899
His lips and cheeks turned white.

95
00:06:51,580 --> 00:06:52,580
Quite white.

96
00:06:52,820 --> 00:06:54,059
I should kill you.

97
00:06:54,600 --> 00:06:55,600
I am killing you.

98
00:06:56,220 --> 00:07:01,080
Your words are such as ought not to be used, violent, unfeminine and untrue.

99
00:07:01,820 --> 00:07:04,139
They betray an unfortunate state of mind.

100
00:07:04,660 --> 00:07:06,199
They marry its severe reproof.

101
00:07:06,740 --> 00:07:12,259
They would seem inexcusable, but that it is the duty of man to forgive his fellow,

102
00:07:12,860 --> 00:07:14,860
even until seventy and seven times.

103
00:07:16,279 --> 00:07:18,220
I had finished the business now.

104
00:07:19,199 --> 00:07:23,660
While earnestly wishing to erase from his mind the trace of my former offense,

105
00:07:24,440 --> 00:07:28,419
I had stamped on that tenacious surface another and far deeper impression.

106
00:07:29,619 --> 00:07:31,080
I had burnt it in.

107
00:07:32,119 --> 00:07:34,740
Now you will indeed hate me, I said.

108
00:07:35,539 --> 00:07:37,619
It is useless to attempt to conciliate you.

109
00:07:38,380 --> 00:07:40,520
I see I have made an eternal enemy of you.

110
00:07:41,460 --> 00:07:48,120
A fresh wrong did these words inflict, the worse, because they touched on the truth.

111
00:07:48,300 --> 00:07:50,820
That bloodless lip quivered to a temporary spasm.

112
00:07:51,559 --> 00:07:53,940
I knew the steely eye I had wetted.

113
00:07:54,759 --> 00:07:55,779
I was heart-wrung.

114
00:07:57,039 --> 00:08:01,960
You utterly misinterpret my words, I said, at once seizing his hand.

115
00:08:02,559 --> 00:08:04,800
I have no intention to grieve or pain you.

116
00:08:05,300 --> 00:08:06,300
Indeed I have not.

117
00:08:07,360 --> 00:08:08,800
Most bitterly he smiled.

118
00:08:09,679 --> 00:08:11,919
Most decidedly he withdrew his hand from mine.

119
00:08:13,059 --> 00:08:17,199
And now you recall your promise and will not go to India at all, I presume.

120
00:08:17,899 --> 00:08:20,240
Said he, after a considerable pause.

121
00:08:20,960 --> 00:08:24,419
Yes, I will, as your assistant, I answered.

122
00:08:25,600 --> 00:08:27,619
A very long silence succeeded.

123
00:08:28,919 --> 00:08:32,600
What struggle there was in him between nature and grace in this interval,

124
00:08:33,199 --> 00:08:34,199
I cannot tell.

125
00:08:34,820 --> 00:08:37,642
Only singular gleams scintillated in his eyes,

126
00:08:37,644 --> 00:08:41,240
and strange shadows passed over his face.

127
00:08:41,529 --> 00:08:42,699
He spoke at last.

128
00:08:43,699 --> 00:08:48,380
I before proved to you the absurdity of a single woman of

129
00:08:48,380 --> 00:08:52,679
your age proposing to accompany abroad a single man of mine.

130
00:08:53,259 --> 00:08:57,228
I proved it to you in such terms as I should have thought

131
00:08:57,229 --> 00:09:01,279
would have prevented you ever again alluding to the plan.

132
00:09:02,179 --> 00:09:05,559
That you have done so I regret for your sake.

133
00:09:06,279 --> 00:09:07,339
I interrupted him.

134
00:09:08,139 --> 00:09:11,399
Anything like a tangible reproach gave me courage at once.

135
00:09:13,300 --> 00:09:15,020
Keep to common sense, engine.

136
00:09:15,919 --> 00:09:17,039
You are verging on nonsense.

137
00:09:17,820 --> 00:09:19,820
You pretend to be shocked by what I have said.

138
00:09:20,779 --> 00:09:22,100
You are not really shocked.

139
00:09:22,600 --> 00:09:26,304
For, with your superior mind, you cannot be either so

140
00:09:26,305 --> 00:09:29,080
dull or so conceited as to misunderstand my meaning.

141
00:09:30,119 --> 00:09:33,960
I say again, I will be your curate if you like.

142
00:09:34,679 --> 00:09:35,820
But never your wife.

143
00:09:36,919 --> 00:09:38,820
Again, he turned lividly pale.

144
00:09:39,559 --> 00:09:44,880
But as before, controlled his passion perfectly, he answered emphatically but calmly.

145
00:09:45,259 --> 00:09:49,919
A female curate, who is not my wife, would never suit me.

146
00:09:50,860 --> 00:09:53,580
With me then it seems you cannot go.

147
00:09:54,320 --> 00:09:58,039
But if you are sincere in your offer, I will, while in town,

148
00:09:58,040 --> 00:10:02,020
speak to a married missionary whose wife needs a cajuta.

149
00:10:03,119 --> 00:10:06,880
Your own fortune will make you independent of the society's aid.

150
00:10:07,880 --> 00:10:11,994
And thus, you may still be spared the dishonor of breaking

151
00:10:11,995 --> 00:10:15,559
your promise and deserting the band you engaged to join.

152
00:10:17,240 --> 00:10:21,527
Now I never had, as the reader knows, either given

153
00:10:21,528 --> 00:10:25,240
any formal promise or entered into any engagement.

154
00:10:25,820 --> 00:10:31,240
And this language was all much too hard and much too despotic for the occasion.

155
00:10:32,039 --> 00:10:39,141
I replied, there is no dishonor, no breach of promise, no desertion in the case.

156
00:10:39,179 --> 00:10:44,220
I am not under the slightest obligation to go to India, especially with strangers.

157
00:10:45,139 --> 00:10:50,839
With you, I would have ventured much because I admire, confide in, and as a

158
00:10:50,841 --> 00:10:56,339
sister, I love you, but I am convinced that go when and with whom I would,

159
00:10:57,119 --> 00:10:59,020
I should not live long in that climate.

160
00:11:00,600 --> 00:11:05,660
Ah, you are afraid of yourself, he said, curling his lip.

161
00:11:06,380 --> 00:11:12,100
I am, God did not give me my life to throw away and to do as you wish me would,

162
00:11:12,880 --> 00:11:17,279
I begin to think, be almost equivalent to committing suicide.

163
00:11:18,320 --> 00:11:24,419
Moreover, before I definitively resolve on quitting England, I will know for certain

164
00:11:24,421 --> 00:11:30,059
whether I cannot be of greater use by remaining in it than by leaving it.

165
00:11:30,960 --> 00:11:32,000
What do you mean?

166
00:11:33,160 --> 00:11:37,740
It would be fruitless to attempt to explain, but there is a point on which I

167
00:11:37,740 --> 00:11:41,622
have long endured painful doubt, and I can go

168
00:11:41,623 --> 00:11:45,199
nowhere till by some means that doubt is removed.

169
00:11:46,600 --> 00:11:49,740
I know where your heart turns and to what it clings.

170
00:11:50,580 --> 00:11:54,080
The interest you cherish is lawless and unconsecrated.

171
00:11:54,899 --> 00:11:56,720
Long since you ought to have crushed it.

172
00:11:57,539 --> 00:11:59,199
Now you should blush to allude to it.

173
00:11:59,979 --> 00:12:01,059
You think of Mr. Rochester?

174
00:12:01,800 --> 00:12:04,139
It was true, I confessed it by silence.

175
00:12:05,279 --> 00:12:07,360
Are you going to seek, Mr. Rochester?

176
00:12:07,919 --> 00:12:10,179
I must find out what is become of him.

177
00:12:11,360 --> 00:12:17,500
It remains for me then, he said, to remember you in my prayers and to

178
00:12:17,501 --> 00:12:22,600
entreat God for you in all earnestness that you may not indeed become a castaway.

179
00:12:23,339 --> 00:12:29,259
I had thought I recognized in you one of the chosen, but God sees not as man sees.

180
00:12:30,279 --> 00:12:31,380
His will be done.

181
00:12:32,479 --> 00:12:37,320
He opened the gate, passed through it, and strayed away down the Glen.

182
00:12:38,039 --> 00:12:39,619
He was soon out of sight.

183
00:12:41,360 --> 00:12:44,563
On re-entering the parlor, I found Diana

184
00:12:44,565 --> 00:12:48,421
standing at the window looking very thoughtful.

185
00:12:48,960 --> 00:12:51,259
Diana was a great deal taller than I.

186
00:12:52,240 --> 00:12:57,580
She put her hand on my shoulder, and stooping, examined my face.

187
00:12:59,000 --> 00:13:04,440
Jane, she said, you are always agitated and pale now.

188
00:13:05,360 --> 00:13:07,059
I am sure there is something the matter.

189
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:10,960
Tell me what business, Sinjin, and you have on hands.

190
00:13:11,639 --> 00:13:14,460
I have watched you this half hour from the window.

191
00:13:15,139 --> 00:13:17,460
You must forgive my being such a spy.

192
00:13:18,179 --> 00:13:21,440
But for a long time I have fancied I hardly know what.

193
00:13:22,160 --> 00:13:23,839
Sinjin is a strange being.

194
00:13:24,649 --> 00:13:25,649
She paused.

195
00:13:26,020 --> 00:13:27,119
I did not speak.

196
00:13:27,839 --> 00:13:29,139
Soon she resumed.

197
00:13:30,240 --> 00:13:34,660
That brother of mine cherishes peculiar views of some sort respecting you,

198
00:13:34,899 --> 00:13:35,899
I am sure.

199
00:13:36,179 --> 00:13:39,139
He has long distinguished you by a notice and interest.

200
00:13:39,339 --> 00:13:42,100
He never showed to anyone else, to what end.

201
00:13:42,899 --> 00:13:43,979
I wish he loved you.

202
00:13:44,479 --> 00:13:45,479
Does he, Jane?

203
00:13:46,580 --> 00:13:48,960
I put her cool hand to my hot forehead.

204
00:13:49,919 --> 00:13:51,880
No, die, not one wit.

205
00:13:52,960 --> 00:13:58,800
Then why does he follow you so with his eyes and get you so frequently alone with

206
00:13:58,801 --> 00:14:01,800
him, and keep you so continually at his side?

207
00:14:03,320 --> 00:14:05,139
Mary and I had both concluded.

208
00:14:05,759 --> 00:14:07,100
He wished you to marry him.

209
00:14:08,639 --> 00:14:09,639
He does.

210
00:14:10,039 --> 00:14:11,820
He has asked me to be his wife.

211
00:14:12,779 --> 00:14:14,080
Diana clapped her hands.

212
00:14:14,699 --> 00:14:16,839
That is just what we hoped and thought.

213
00:14:17,679 --> 00:14:19,559
And you will marry him, Jane, won't you?

214
00:14:20,380 --> 00:14:22,080
And then he will stay in England.

215
00:14:23,639 --> 00:14:27,888
Far from that Diana, his sole idea in proposing to me is

216
00:14:27,888 --> 00:14:31,740
to procure a fitting fellow laborer in his Indian toils.

217
00:14:32,520 --> 00:14:33,520
What?

218
00:14:33,800 --> 00:14:35,259
He wishes you to go to India?

219
00:14:36,240 --> 00:14:37,240
Yes.

220
00:14:38,119 --> 00:14:39,899
Madness, she exclaimed.

221
00:14:43,460 --> 00:14:45,100
You never shall go.

222
00:14:45,699 --> 00:14:47,339
You have not consented, have you, Jane?

223
00:14:48,279 --> 00:14:54,501
I have refused to marry him and have consequently displeased him, she suggested.

224
00:14:54,940 --> 00:14:58,259
Deeply, he will never forgive me, I fear,

225
00:14:58,260 --> 00:15:01,980
yet I offered to accompany him as his sister.

226
00:15:02,820 --> 00:15:05,039
It was frantic, folly, to do so, Jane.

227
00:15:05,960 --> 00:15:09,220
Think of the task you undertook, one of incessant

228
00:15:09,221 --> 00:15:12,139
fatigue, where fatigue kills even the strong.

229
00:15:13,220 --> 00:15:14,220
And you are weak.

230
00:15:14,940 --> 00:15:19,479
Sinjin, you know him, would urge you to impossibilities.

231
00:15:20,259 --> 00:15:24,460
With him, there would be no permission to rest during the hot hours.

232
00:15:25,020 --> 00:15:31,260
And unfortunately, I have noticed, whatever he exacts, you force yourself to perform.

233
00:15:31,820 --> 00:15:35,399
I am astonished you found courage to refuse his hand.

234
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:37,240
You do not love him then, Jane.

235
00:15:37,919 --> 00:15:41,339
Not as a husband, yet he is a handsome fellow.

236
00:15:42,080 --> 00:15:45,600
And I am so plain you see, die, we should never suit.

237
00:15:46,639 --> 00:15:48,380
Plain, you, not at all.

238
00:15:49,100 --> 00:15:53,440
You are much too pretty, as well as too good, to be grilled alive in Calcutta.

239
00:15:54,660 --> 00:15:57,440
And again, she earnestly conjured me to give

240
00:15:57,441 --> 00:16:01,100
up all thoughts of going out with her brother.

241
00:16:01,440 --> 00:16:03,559
I must indeed, I said.

242
00:16:04,460 --> 00:16:08,233
For when just now I repeated the offer of serving him for a

243
00:16:08,235 --> 00:16:12,380
deacon, he expressed himself shocked at my want of decency.

244
00:16:13,500 --> 00:16:18,059
He seemed to think I had committed an impropriety in proposing to accompany him

245
00:16:18,061 --> 00:16:23,820
unmarried, as if I had not from the first hope to find in him a brother,

246
00:16:24,520 --> 00:16:26,619
and habitually regarded him as such.

247
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:30,800
What makes you say he does not love you Jane?

248
00:16:31,839 --> 00:16:33,899
You should hear himself on the subject.

249
00:16:34,899 --> 00:16:37,860
He has again and again explained that it is

250
00:16:37,861 --> 00:16:41,701
not himself, but his office he wishes to mate.

251
00:16:42,339 --> 00:16:48,240
He has told me, I am formed for labor, not for love, which is true, no doubt.

252
00:16:49,020 --> 00:16:52,449
But in my opinion, if I am not formed for love,

253
00:16:52,451 --> 00:16:56,201
it follows that I am not formed for marriage.

254
00:16:56,399 --> 00:16:58,793
Would it not be strange, DA, to be chained for life,

255
00:16:58,793 --> 00:17:01,441
to a man who regarded one but as a useful tool?

256
00:17:03,240 --> 00:17:05,220
Insupportable, unnatural out of the question.

257
00:17:06,699 --> 00:17:09,160
And then, I continued.

258
00:17:10,520 --> 00:17:17,139
Though I have only sisterly affection for him now, yet, if forced to be his wife,

259
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:22,419
I can imagine the possibility of conceiving an inevitable, strange,

260
00:17:22,720 --> 00:17:27,880
torturing kind of love for him, because he is so talented, and there is

261
00:17:27,880 --> 00:17:32,800
often a certain heroic grandeur in his look, manner, and conversation.

262
00:17:33,940 --> 00:17:37,880
In that case, my lot would become unspeakably wretched.

263
00:17:38,679 --> 00:17:40,279
He would not want me to love him.

264
00:17:40,779 --> 00:17:45,460
And if I showed the feeling, he would make me sensible that it was a superfluity,

265
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:48,619
unrequired by him, unbecoming in me.

266
00:17:49,339 --> 00:17:50,539
I know he would.

267
00:17:52,059 --> 00:17:54,720
And yet, Sinjin is a good man, said Diana.

268
00:17:55,600 --> 00:18:00,520
He is a good and a great man, but he forgets pitilessly the feelings and claims

269
00:18:00,520 --> 00:18:03,600
of little people in pursuing his own large views.

270
00:18:04,759 --> 00:18:09,179
It is better therefore, for the insignificant to keep out of his way,

271
00:18:09,180 --> 00:18:12,759
lest, in his progress, he should trample them down.

272
00:18:14,119 --> 00:18:15,119
Here he comes.

273
00:18:16,039 --> 00:18:17,600
I will leave you, Diana.

274
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:22,626
And I hastened upstairs as I saw him entering the

275
00:18:22,626 --> 00:18:25,740
garden, but I was forced to meet him again at supper.

276
00:18:26,720 --> 00:18:30,000
During that meal, he appeared just as composed as usual.

277
00:18:30,699 --> 00:18:33,520
I had thought he would hardly speak to me.

278
00:18:34,300 --> 00:18:38,360
And I was certain he had given up the pursuit of his matrimonial scheme.

279
00:18:39,259 --> 00:18:42,380
The sequel showed I was mistaken on both points.

280
00:18:43,339 --> 00:18:46,220
He addressed me precisely in his ordinary manner.

281
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:50,399
Or what had, of late, been his ordinary manner.

282
00:18:51,039 --> 00:18:52,639
One scrupulously polite.

283
00:18:53,600 --> 00:18:56,638
No doubt he had invoked the help of the Holy

284
00:18:56,639 --> 00:18:59,861
Spirit to subdue the anger I had roused in him.

285
00:19:00,399 --> 00:19:03,000
And now believed he had forgiven me once more.

286
00:19:04,520 --> 00:19:11,120
For the evening reading before prayers, he selected the 21st chapter of Revelation.

287
00:19:12,100 --> 00:19:14,947
It was at all times pleasant to listen, while

288
00:19:14,948 --> 00:19:18,561
from his lips fell the words of the Bible.

289
00:19:19,259 --> 00:19:23,580
Never did his fine voice sound at once so sweet and full.

290
00:19:24,759 --> 00:19:28,434
Never did his manner become so impressive in its noble

291
00:19:28,436 --> 00:19:31,399
simplicity as when he delivered the oracles of God.

292
00:19:32,179 --> 00:19:38,720
And tonight, that voice took a more solemn tone, that manner a more thrilling meaning

293
00:19:38,721 --> 00:19:44,440
as he sat in the midst of his household circle, the May moon shining in through

294
00:19:44,441 --> 00:19:47,247
the uncut and window and rendering almost

295
00:19:47,248 --> 00:19:50,460
unnecessary the light of the candle on the table.

296
00:19:51,020 --> 00:19:58,240
As he sat there, bending over the great old Bible, and described from its page the

297
00:19:58,240 --> 00:20:03,179
vision of the new heaven and the new earth, told how God would come to dwell

298
00:20:03,180 --> 00:20:10,039
with men, how he would wipe away all tears from their eyes, and promised that there

299
00:20:10,040 --> 00:20:15,440
should be no more death, neither sorrow nor crying, nor any more pain,

300
00:20:16,100 --> 00:20:18,259
because the former things were passed away.

301
00:20:19,179 --> 00:20:24,440
The succeeding words thrilled me strangely as he spoke them, especially as I felt by

302
00:20:24,441 --> 00:20:28,168
the slight indescribable alteration in sound,

303
00:20:28,168 --> 00:20:32,020
that in uttering them, his eye had turned on me.

304
00:20:33,580 --> 00:20:38,059
He that overcomeeth shall inherit all things, and I will be his God,

305
00:20:38,860 --> 00:20:43,220
and he shall be my son, but was slowly, distinctly

306
00:20:43,221 --> 00:20:46,380
read, the fearful, the unbelieving, etc.

307
00:20:47,100 --> 00:20:50,759
She'll have their part in the lake, which burneth with fire and brimstone,

308
00:20:51,380 --> 00:20:52,440
which is the second death.

309
00:20:53,800 --> 00:20:58,880
Hence forward, I knew what fate Shingin feared for me.

310
00:20:59,800 --> 00:21:05,179
A calm, subdued triumph, blent with a longing earnestness, marked his

311
00:21:05,180 --> 00:21:08,479
enunciation of the last glorious verses of that chapter.

312
00:21:09,460 --> 00:21:13,880
The reader believed his name was already written in the Lamb's book of life,

313
00:21:14,679 --> 00:21:20,339
and he yearned after the hour which should admit him to the city, to which the kings

314
00:21:20,341 --> 00:21:26,779
of the earth bring their glory and honor, which has no need of sun or moon to shine

315
00:21:26,781 --> 00:21:32,979
in it, because the glory of God lightens it, and the Lamb is the light thereof.

316
00:21:33,520 --> 00:21:39,839
In the prayer following the chapter, all his stern zeal woke.

317
00:21:40,720 --> 00:21:45,839
He was in deep earnest, wrestling with God, and resolved on a conquest.

318
00:21:46,839 --> 00:21:52,880
He supplicated strength for the weak hearted, guidance for wanderers from the fold.

319
00:21:53,139 --> 00:21:58,779
A return, even at the eleventh hour, for those whom the temptations of the

320
00:21:58,781 --> 00:22:02,220
world and the flesh were luring from the narrow path.

321
00:22:03,100 --> 00:22:07,979
He asked, he urged, he claimed the boon of a brand snatched from the burning.

322
00:22:09,039 --> 00:22:10,899
Ernestness is ever deeply solemn.

323
00:22:11,679 --> 00:22:15,059
First, as I listened to that prayer, I wondered at his.

324
00:22:16,119 --> 00:22:21,820
Then, when it continued in rows, I was touched by it, and at last awed.

325
00:22:22,520 --> 00:22:26,625
He felt the greatness and goodness of his purpose so sincerely,

326
00:22:26,626 --> 00:22:31,059
others who heard him plead for it could not but feel it too.

327
00:22:31,839 --> 00:22:34,899
The prayer over, we took leave of him.

328
00:22:35,639 --> 00:22:38,199
He was to go at a very early hour in the morning.

329
00:22:39,320 --> 00:22:42,460
Diana and Mary, having kissed him, left the room.

330
00:22:43,399 --> 00:22:47,440
In compliance, I think, with a whispered hint from him.

331
00:22:48,520 --> 00:22:52,360
I tended my hand, and wished him a pleasant journey.

332
00:22:53,360 --> 00:22:57,919
Thank you, Jane, as I said, I shall return from Cambridge in a fortnight.

333
00:22:58,559 --> 00:23:01,339
That space then is yet left you for reflection.

334
00:23:02,500 --> 00:23:07,539
If I listened to human pride, I should say no more to you of marriage with me.

335
00:23:08,380 --> 00:23:13,279
But I listened to my duty, and keep steadily in view my first aim.

336
00:23:13,979 --> 00:23:16,399
To do all things to the glory of God.

337
00:23:17,279 --> 00:23:18,740
My master was long suffering.

338
00:23:19,479 --> 00:23:20,479
So will I be?

339
00:23:20,940 --> 00:23:25,759
I cannot give you up to perdition as a vessel of wrath, repent, resolve,

340
00:23:26,440 --> 00:23:27,720
while there is yet time.

341
00:23:28,199 --> 00:23:31,725
Remember, we are bid to work while it is day,

342
00:23:31,725 --> 00:23:35,281
warned that the night come when no man shall work.

343
00:23:36,320 --> 00:23:40,580
Remember the fate of Divas, who had his good things in this life.

344
00:23:41,460 --> 00:23:48,040
God give you strength to choose that better part, which shall not be taken from you.

345
00:23:48,080 --> 00:23:53,619
He laid his hand on my head, as he uttered the last words, he had spoken earnestly,

346
00:23:53,800 --> 00:23:54,800
mildly.

347
00:23:55,100 --> 00:24:00,880
His look was not indeed that of a lover beholding his mistress, but it was that of

348
00:24:00,880 --> 00:24:07,100
a pastor, recalling his wandering sheep, or better of a guardian angel,

349
00:24:07,100 --> 00:24:10,320
watching the soul for which he is responsible.

350
00:24:11,279 --> 00:24:16,600
All men of talent, whether they be men of feeling or not, whether they be zealots,

351
00:24:16,699 --> 00:24:20,448
or aspirants, or despots, provided only they be sincere,

352
00:24:20,449 --> 00:24:24,779
have their sublime moments, when they subdue and rule.

353
00:24:26,020 --> 00:24:30,751
I felt veneration for sin, veneration so strong that its

354
00:24:30,751 --> 00:24:34,940
impetus thrust me at once to the point I had so long shunned.

355
00:24:35,419 --> 00:24:41,220
I was tempted to cease struggling with him, to rush down the torrent of his will

356
00:24:41,221 --> 00:24:45,059
into the gulf of his existence, and there lose my own.

357
00:24:46,279 --> 00:24:49,683
I was almost as hard beset by him now, as I had

358
00:24:49,683 --> 00:24:53,220
been once before, in a different way, by another.

359
00:24:53,940 --> 00:24:58,899
I was a fool both times, to have yielded then would have been an error of

360
00:24:58,900 --> 00:25:03,160
principle, to have yielded now would have been an error of judgment.

361
00:25:04,240 --> 00:25:10,500
So I think at this hour, when I look back to the crisis through the quiet medium of

362
00:25:10,501 --> 00:25:14,039
time, I was unconscious of folly at the instant.

363
00:25:15,119 --> 00:25:19,940
I stood motionless under my harifants' touch, my refusals were forgotten,

364
00:25:20,619 --> 00:25:26,600
my fears overcome, my wrestling's paralyzed, the impossible, i.e.

365
00:25:26,601 --> 00:25:31,820
, my marriage with singeon, was fast becoming the possible, or was changing

366
00:25:31,820 --> 00:25:38,080
utterly with a sudden sweep, religion called, angels beckoned, god commanded,

367
00:25:38,639 --> 00:25:44,441
life rolled together like a scroll, death's gates opening, showed eternity beyond.

368
00:25:44,940 --> 00:25:50,119
It seemed that for safety and bliss there all here might be sacrificed in a second.

369
00:25:51,399 --> 00:25:53,500
The dim room was full of visions.

370
00:25:54,179 --> 00:25:56,639
Could you decide now, ask the missionary?

371
00:25:57,500 --> 00:25:59,119
The inquiry was put in gentle tones.

372
00:25:59,800 --> 00:26:01,100
He drew me to him as gently.

373
00:26:02,139 --> 00:26:03,139
Oh, that gentleness!

374
00:26:03,679 --> 00:26:06,119
How far more potent is it than force?

375
00:26:07,020 --> 00:26:08,720
I could resist Shingen's wrath.

376
00:26:09,399 --> 00:26:11,639
I grew planned as a reed under his kindness.

377
00:26:12,699 --> 00:26:13,899
Yet I knew all the time.

378
00:26:14,660 --> 00:26:17,320
If I yielded now, I should not the less be

379
00:26:17,320 --> 00:26:20,760
made to repent someday of my former rebellion.

380
00:26:21,740 --> 00:26:25,479
His nature was not changed by one hour of solemn prayer.

381
00:26:26,300 --> 00:26:27,660
It was only elevated.

382
00:26:29,139 --> 00:26:33,080
I could decide if I were but certain, I answered, where I

383
00:26:33,081 --> 00:26:36,039
but convinced that it is God's will, I should marry you.

384
00:26:36,460 --> 00:26:38,639
I could vow to marry you here and now.

385
00:26:39,240 --> 00:26:40,860
Come afterwards, what would?

386
00:26:41,679 --> 00:26:43,539
My prayers are heard.

387
00:26:44,539 --> 00:26:45,800
It jackulated Shingen.

388
00:26:46,380 --> 00:26:50,220
He pressed his hand firmer on my head, as if he claimed me.

389
00:26:50,940 --> 00:26:54,020
He surrounded me with his arm almost as if he loved me.

390
00:26:54,479 --> 00:26:56,399
I say almost, I knew the difference.

391
00:26:57,259 --> 00:26:59,320
For I had felt what it was to be loved.

392
00:26:59,979 --> 00:27:05,339
But like him, I had now put love out of the question and thought only of duty.

393
00:27:06,160 --> 00:27:10,979
I contended with my inward dimness of vision before which clouds yet rolled.

394
00:27:11,660 --> 00:27:16,520
I sincerely, deeply, fervently longed to do what was right.

395
00:27:17,300 --> 00:27:18,300
And only that.

396
00:27:18,880 --> 00:27:21,919
Show me, show me the path I entreated of heaven.

397
00:27:22,639 --> 00:27:26,838
I was excited more than I had ever been, and whether what

398
00:27:26,839 --> 00:27:30,919
followed was the effect of excitement, the reader shall judge.

399
00:27:31,940 --> 00:27:35,870
All the house was still, for I believe all except

400
00:27:35,872 --> 00:27:39,880
Shingen and myself were now retired to rest.

401
00:27:40,419 --> 00:27:44,286
The one candle was dying out, the room was full of

402
00:27:44,288 --> 00:27:48,300
moonlight, my heart beat fast and thick, I heard its throb.

403
00:27:49,440 --> 00:27:54,080
Suddenly, it stood still to an inexpressible feeling that thrilled it

404
00:27:54,081 --> 00:27:57,699
through, and passed at once to my head and extremities.

405
00:27:58,580 --> 00:28:03,380
The feeling was not like an electric shock, but it was quite as sharp,

406
00:28:04,059 --> 00:28:06,100
as strange, as startling.

407
00:28:07,279 --> 00:28:12,679
It acted on my senses as if their utmost activity hitherto had been but torper,

408
00:28:13,279 --> 00:28:15,940
from which they were now summoned and forced to wake.

409
00:28:16,820 --> 00:28:22,000
They rose expectant, eye and ear waited while the flesh quivered on my bones.

410
00:28:23,500 --> 00:28:24,500
What have you heard?

411
00:28:25,100 --> 00:28:26,880
What do you see?" asked Shingen.

412
00:28:28,000 --> 00:28:33,580
I saw nothing, but I heard a voice somewhere cry, jane, jane, jane, nothing more.

413
00:28:33,940 --> 00:28:34,940
Oh, God!

414
00:28:35,300 --> 00:28:36,759
What is it, I gasped?

415
00:28:37,479 --> 00:28:39,839
I might have said, where is it?

416
00:28:40,520 --> 00:28:44,800
For it did not seem in the room, nor in the house, nor in the garden.

417
00:28:45,520 --> 00:28:49,660
It did not come out of the air, nor from under the earth, nor from overhead.

418
00:28:50,220 --> 00:28:54,360
I had heard it, where or whence, forever impossible to know.

419
00:28:55,039 --> 00:28:59,660
And it was the voice of a human being, a known, loved, well-remembered voice,

420
00:28:59,660 --> 00:29:06,179
that of Edward Fairfax Rochester, and its spoken pain and woe, wildly,

421
00:29:06,720 --> 00:29:07,839
eerily, urgently.

422
00:29:08,399 --> 00:29:09,520
I am coming, I cried.

423
00:29:10,279 --> 00:29:10,740
Wait for me!

424
00:29:10,979 --> 00:29:11,979
Oh, I will come!

425
00:29:12,580 --> 00:29:14,979
I flew to the door and looked into the passage.

426
00:29:15,740 --> 00:29:16,100
It was dark.

427
00:29:16,559 --> 00:29:17,600
I ran out into the garden.

428
00:29:18,000 --> 00:29:19,000
It was void.

429
00:29:19,240 --> 00:29:20,699
Where are you, I exclaimed?

430
00:29:21,759 --> 00:29:24,960
The hills beyond Marsh Glen sent the answer faintly back.

431
00:29:26,800 --> 00:29:27,899
Where are you?

432
00:29:28,500 --> 00:29:29,500
I listened.

433
00:29:29,919 --> 00:29:34,940
The windside low in the furs, all was molland loneliness and midnight hush.

434
00:29:36,199 --> 00:29:39,692
Down superstition, I commented, as that specter

435
00:29:39,694 --> 00:29:42,561
rose up black by the black you at the gate.

436
00:29:43,460 --> 00:29:46,300
This is not thy deception, nor thy witchcraft.

437
00:29:47,080 --> 00:29:48,240
It is the work of nature.

438
00:29:49,220 --> 00:29:52,740
She was roused, and did, no miracle, but her best.

439
00:29:53,580 --> 00:29:57,479
I broke from Sinjin, who had followed, and would have detained me.

440
00:29:58,279 --> 00:30:00,720
It was my time to assume ascendancy.

441
00:30:01,399 --> 00:30:03,360
My powers were in play and in force.

442
00:30:04,360 --> 00:30:06,240
I told him to forebear question or remark.

443
00:30:07,020 --> 00:30:08,240
I desired him to leave me.

444
00:30:08,899 --> 00:30:10,660
I must, and would be alone.

445
00:30:11,699 --> 00:30:12,699
He obeyed at once.

446
00:30:13,820 --> 00:30:17,839
Where there is energy to command well enough, obedience never fails.

447
00:30:18,860 --> 00:30:25,460
I mounted to my chamber, locked myself in, fell on my knees, and prayed in my way,

448
00:30:25,880 --> 00:30:29,160
a different way to Sinjin's, but effective in its own fashion.

449
00:30:30,440 --> 00:30:34,160
I seemed to penetrate very near a mighty spirit,

450
00:30:34,161 --> 00:30:37,600
and my soul rushed out in gratitude at his feet.

451
00:30:38,940 --> 00:30:46,360
I rose from the Thanksgiving, took a resolve, and lay down, unscared,

452
00:30:46,940 --> 00:30:50,000
enlightened, eager, but for the daylight.
